The source code, documentation, trained model files and other material in this
repository (the "Software") are made publicly visible so that people can see the
author's work. Being visible does not make the Software open source.

1. THE ONLY PERMITTED USES

   a. Viewing. Anyone may read and browse the Software, for example on GitHub.

   b. Evaluation. Instructors, examiners, reviewers and prospective employers or
      collaborators may download, install and run the Software, only in order to
      evaluate the author's work.

   c. Personal learning. Individuals may run and modify a private copy of the
      Software for their own non-commercial study, using footage they recorded
      themselves or are otherwise allowed to use.

   Each of these is subject to section 3.

2. EVERYTHING ELSE IS FORBIDDEN

   Any use not listed in section 1 is not permitted. This includes, but is not
   limited to:

   a. redistributing the Software, in whole or in part, modified or not, including
      publishing copies, forks or mirrors outside GitHub's own fork feature;
   b. commercial use of any kind, including in a product or service;
   c. deploying the Software on real camera feeds or streams, or running it on
      footage for any purpose other than those in section 1;
   d. using the Software, any part of it, or data it produces in another project,
      product, service or publication.

3. PROHIBITED USES

   Even within section 1, the Software and any data it produces must never be used
   to:

   a. stalk, follow, track or monitor a specific person or their vehicle;
   b. harass, intimidate, threaten, blackmail or otherwise harm any person;
   c. build profiles of individuals, such as their movements, habits, locations or
      associations;
   d. carry out covert or mass surveillance of any place;
   e. discriminate against or target people because of ethnicity, religion,
      political opinion, gender, sexual orientation, disability or any other
      protected characteristic, or target journalists, activists or protesters;
   f. sell, share or publish plate sightings or movement data tied to identifiable
      people, or combine them with other data to identify people;
   g. break any privacy or data-protection law, including KVKK (Turkey, Law
      No. 6698) and the GDPR (EU) or local law.

   See RESPONSIBLE_USE.md for the full policy.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

   The Software depends on third-party libraries and models that keep their own
   licenses, listed in SOURCES.md. This license covers only the author's own work. It
   does not change or override any third-party license. Anyone who uses the Software
   must also comply with those licenses.

5. TERMINATION

   Any use outside section 1, or any use listed in section 3, ends all rights granted
   by this license immediately and automatically.

6. NO WARRANTY, NO LIABILITY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.
